 "name": "Mountain Stream Facilities: Preference and Captions (CEM)",
 "description": "Faithful replication of the online survey in Peng, Huang & Chen (2022), Water 14:3605. Participants see 22 photographs of check dams, ground sills, embankments and ecological channels from two award-winning stream renovation projects in Taiwan (Toubiankeng Stream in Zhongpu and Sijiaolin Stream). For each picture they rate their scenic preference from 1 to 5 and write three short captions following the caption evaluation method (CEM): the element they notice, its feature (form, colour, arrangement…) and the feeling it gives. Analysis: mean preference per picture and per project; captions coded into keywords and summarised as the top three elements, representations and perceptions per picture. Each trial records the project site and the picture's mean preference in the paper.\n\nPictures: the 22 photographs printed in the paper's Tables 1 and 2 (CC BY 4.0), used with credit; the template is removed if the authors object.\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) the paper presented the photos as a slide show before an online questionnaire; here each picture is shown on its own page in random order; (2) the exact question wordings, scale anchors and caption prompts are not printed in the paper and were written for this template from its description of the 1–5 preference scale and the three CEM captions; (3) the student-status question and consent are added; (4) the paper's on-site investigation (24 volunteers walking the sites and taking their own photos) is not included; (5) pictures are the small versions printed in the paper (about 233 × 216 px).",
